    "commit": "f879b410a",
    "summary": "A further review of ab51d6839 found three more P2s: the raw (no-RoundWriter) persistence path wrote fresh meta with no lifecycle key at all, so a completed record's stamp was silently dropped and the storage layer's terminal-content check never even saw it; the read-merge-write was not serialized across overlapping calls, so two concurrent appends could drop one addition even though each write was individually serialized; and pass-through-codecs.test.ts's registered-kinds count was stale. Fixed: withStoredModel is now applied unconditionally so both paths carry the stored lifecycle forward (enforcing TerminalArtifactError on a completed record on both paths); the whole read-merge-write is now serialized in-process per (repoPath, epicHash, storyId); the stale test count was corrected to 17. Added tests for both: a real-lifecycle-service completion test and a concurrent-append test."
  },
